From 00e0dde9484babe8cb92deb39c1efd25c66159e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Olivier Cochard <olivier@FreeBSD.org>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 15:34:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] iommu: Identity-map contexts when DMA remapping is disabled

With hw.amdiommu.enable=1 alone, interrupt remapping is on and DMA
remapping is off.  amdiommu_ir_find() still instantiates a context for
each MSI source, and it got a translating domain with an empty page
table while busdma kept handing out physical addresses, so every DMA
from these devices faulted.  On a Ryzen 7 7735HS the USB devices
attached in an endless loop.

Treat a unit with DMA remapping disabled like a device with remapping
disabled: give the context the identity mapping.

Fixes:		0f5116d7efe3 ("AMD IOMMU driver")
MFC after:	1 week
---
 sys/dev/iommu/busdma_iommu.c | 9 ++++++---
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sys/dev/iommu/busdma_iommu.c b/sys/dev/iommu/busdma_iommu.c
index 3852429c4a8a..62fda6143892 100644
--- a/sys/dev/iommu/busdma_iommu.c
+++ b/sys/dev/iommu/busdma_iommu.c
@@ -261,10 +261,13 @@ iommu_instantiate_ctx(struct iommu_unit *unit, device_t dev, bool rmrr)
 	 * cannot disable the IOMMU unit, due to possibility of other
 	 * devices on the same IOMMU unit still requiring translation.
 	 * Instead provide the identity mapping for the device
-	 * context.
+	 * context.  Do the same when DMA remapping is disabled for
+	 * the unit: busdma then does not use the context, but
+	 * interrupt remapping might still create it.
 	 */
-	disabled = iommu_bus_dma_is_dev_disabled(pci_get_domain(requester),
-	    pci_get_bus(requester), pci_get_slot(requester), 
+	disabled = !unit->dma_enabled ||
+	    iommu_bus_dma_is_dev_disabled(pci_get_domain(requester),
+	    pci_get_bus(requester), pci_get_slot(requester),
 	    pci_get_function(requester));
 	ctx = iommu_get_ctx(unit, requester, rid, disabled, rmrr);
 	if (ctx == NULL)
